UID:1012675
DESCRIPTION:<p>2007. A mysterious photo album arrives at the U.S. Holocaus
 t Memorial Museum. Nazi-era images unlike any that have been seen before. 
 A relentless search begins into the history trapped in the lens. As the al
 bum makes headlines\, questions surface that ignite a worldwide reckoning.
  Based on true events\, <em>Here There Are Blueberries</em> tells the stor
 y of these historical photographs&mdash\;what they reveal about the perpet
 rators of the Holocaust\, and our own humanity.<br /><br /><em>Here There 
 Are Blueberries</em> is the Pulitzer Prize Finalist that the Los Angeles T
 imes calls &ldquo\;the greatest detective story ever told.&rdquo\; From Te
 ctonic Theater Project (<em>The Laramie Project</em>)\, conceived and dire
 cted by Mois&eacute\;s Kaufman\, and written by Kaufman and Amanda Gronich
 \, <em>Here There Are Blueberries</em> is &ldquo\;riveting&rdquo\; (<em>Th
 e Washington Post</em>)\, &ldquo\;unforgettable&rdquo\; (<em>The Guardian<
 /em>)\, and &ldquo\;one of the finest new plays of the year&rdquo\; (<em>T
 he Wall Street Journal</em>).<br /><br />&ldquo\;Precise and intelligent &
 ndash\; <em>Here There Are Blueberries</em> looks at its subject from an u
 nusual angle.&rdquo\; - Jesse Green\, <em>The New York Times</em><br /><br
  />&ldquo\;<em>Here There Are Blueberries</em> makes the painstaking work 
 of historical inquiry seem like the greatest detective story ever written.
 &rdquo\; - Charles McNulty\, <em>Los Angeles Times</em><br /><br />&ldquo\
 ;FIVE STARS - This searing drama builds into an unforgettable inquiry\, pl
 aying out like a profound\, innovative and unique detective drama.&rdquo\;
  - Arifa Akbar\, <em>The Guardian</em><br /><br />&ldquo\;<em>Blueberries<
 /em> artfully tells the true tale of the pictures and their march through 
 public consciousness.&rdquo\; - Vinson Cunningham\, <em>The New Yorker</em
 ><br /><br />&ldquo\;Masterful. Some excellent dramas might give you a phy
 sical chill or two. At <em>Here There Are Blueberries</em>\, you might los
 e count of all the jolts that shoot down your arms.&rdquo\; -Lily Janiak\,
  <em>San Francisco Chronicle</em></p>
LOCATION:Barrymore Theatre\, 243 West 47th Street\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
